steps.body:
Rope $(4,2)\to(6,2)$ and rope $(2,4)\to(2,6)$ (each through three poles). They create:

- bottom-right plot $(4,2),(6,2),(6,6),(2,6),(2,4)$: a $4\times4$ square with a corner cut by legs 2;
- top-right plot $(4,0),(5,0),(6,1),(6,2),(4,2)$: a $2\times2$ square with a corner cut by legs 1;
- bottom-left plot $(0,4),(2,4),(2,6),(1,6),(0,5)$: a $2\times2$ square with a corner cut by legs 1.

```c
prev = NULL; cur = head;
while (cur) { next = cur->next; cur->next = prev; prev = cur; cur = next; }
head = prev;
```
Three pointers ⇒ $O(1)$ space; one pass ⇒ $O(n)$ time.
